[{:seon.task/name "ns-keeps-its-metadata"
  :seon.task/plan "Jolt's `(ns ^:scratch foo)` attaches no metadata to the namespace, so a namespace cannot be declared ^:scratch from the REPL (`seon.program/scratch-ns?` reads `(:scratch (meta nsx))`). Two stopgaps stand in: `seon.agent/make-ns!` sets it with `alter-meta!` and `seon.repl/wrap-record` reapplies the ns form's metadata with alter-meta!. Ran 2026-11-06 at a root: a top-level `(ns ^:scratch x)` shows {:scratch true}, through wrap-record, and `(let [] (eval '(ns ^:scratch y)))`, which it does not see, leaves (meta (find-ns 'y)) nil. On the JVM, `(meta (find-ns 'foo))` holds the ns form's metadata. Cause: Jolt's ns macro (host/chez/ns.ss). Correct, on a `jolt/<topic>` branch: the ns form's metadata (docstring and attr-map too) merges onto the namespace. Deletes both stopgaps (every definition happens once)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.program-test/a-scratch-ns-declared-at-the-repl-stays-scratch}}]
